WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.410
- My next guest is a music icon

00:00:02.410 --> 00:00:04.810
who came down from the
northern reaches of Alaska

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:08.410
to save our souls and sell over
30 million albums worldwide.

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:09.920
Not too shabby.

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:12.150
This year marks the 25th anniversary

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:14.276
of her 12-time platinum, that's right,

00:00:14.276 --> 00:00:17.820
12-time platinum selling
record, "Pieces of You."

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:19.905
Let's say hello to Jewel, everybody!

00:00:19.905 --> 00:00:23.014
(upbeat music)
(audience clapping)

00:00:23.014 --> 00:00:24.860
- [Kelly] Hi.

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:26.870
- Hi, I'm so glad to see
you, you know, virtually.

00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:28.420
- Yeah, I know, you look so cute.

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:30.320
Oh my gosh, I love your
whole style right now.

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:33.970
Oh, well it's the 25th
anniversary of your debut album.

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:38.190
I mean, it's rare when
any artist has an album,

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:40.110
like "Pieces of You," you
know, that kind of effect

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:42.900
on pop culture and that
kind of life-changing event

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:45.960
for one human, like that
changed your life, that album.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:48.560
So how is it looking back on that?

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:50.890
- You know, this album
feels like a magic carpet.

00:00:50.890 --> 00:00:52.440
I mean, I don't know how
many words are on it.

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:55.710
Let's say 1,000, 1,000
words changed my life.

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:58.170
1,000 words got me on the
cover of TIME Magazine

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:01.250
for representing hope
and kind of moving grunge

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:02.720
out into a different era.

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:05.360
It was insane what this record did to me

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:06.980
and how it changed my life.

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:09.140
- Yeah, I think though,
it's because you were so,

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:12.020
like just as a fan, it
was just so pure and raw

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:13.930
and honest and not formulaic,

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:16.070
and it was all the things that were like

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:18.240
I feel like really
needed in that time too,

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:20.390
or every time.

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:22.280
But I felt like you were really different,

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:23.520
and that's what really stood out.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:25.330
And it was beautiful and poetic.

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:27.820
And I don't know, we say
we sang "Foolish Games"

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:30.000
together on your Greatest
Albums Hit, and I,

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.210
or your Greatest Hits album, sorry,

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:34.090
and I played it cool,

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:36.194
but my friend that was
with me at the time,

00:01:36.194 --> 00:01:38.600
I was like, I freaked out after.

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:40.310
Like I was trying to be
really cool in front of you

00:01:40.310 --> 00:01:42.130
and not do what I did with Meryl Streep.

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:45.550
But like I was so excited
that I got to sing on that.

00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:47.390
I mean, singing harmony with
you is the coolest thing.

00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:49.780
You have the sexiest female voice

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:51.610
I've ever heard in my entire life.

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:54.900
Like it's so cool and
poetic and sexy and sweet.

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:56.550
It's so awesome.

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:58.540
- Well, I remember doing
that duet with you,

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:00.260
and I was just, I mean, I know your range,

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:02.850
and I've been a fan of your
voice and of you as a person,

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:04.420
but hearing you sing in person,

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:06.590
when I'm holding out that long note,

00:02:06.590 --> 00:02:08.470
it's the very top of what I have.

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:10.750
It's, that's the roof, that's what I got.

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:12.870
And then you were just
like a good third above it

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:15.354
in your chest voice,
like (imitates singing)

00:02:15.354 --> 00:02:17.304
♪ This is how long she can do it ♪

00:02:17.304 --> 00:02:18.810
♪ I'm just going to hang out a while ♪

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:20.170
It's amazing.

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:21.590
- I wouldn't, no, I'm
gonna be honest with you.

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:22.423
It took all the air.

00:02:22.423 --> 00:02:24.310
I feel like you have
like Celine Dion lungs

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:28.360
and your capacity to hold
out a note is kind of insane.

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:30.360
I was really nervous and
trying to bring my A game.

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:31.310
So I impressed you.

